["大模型应该可以定整体策略,jev管技能释放", "https://ollama.com/library/kev 这类", "看看目前哪个的性能和效果最好", "可以拿他试一下,但是还是要效果和性能好的,而且不能光靠他把,看看现在大家都怎么做的", "升级", "PI的问题解决了吗,pi其他都能用的啊", "派你自己的subagent并行查吧", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae49beb0aba582ebb</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01AGhHoNjTq8BFCdVYZ2XUs3</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/ae49beb0aba582ebb.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Review PiRpcChannel for Unity bugs\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Code Review Summary\n\n**Files reviewed:** 4 (PiRpcChannel.cs, PiHost.cs, AgentCoordinator.cs, GameApp.cs), plus CompanionBrain.cs, NemesisBrain.cs and KevScorer.cs at the call sites, pi's `rpc-mode.ts`, the bot logs, and pi's own session transcript in the isolated home.\n**Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES.** The Unity–pi plumbing works. The bug is in what the model generates, and the code doesn't handle it.\n\nlsp_diagnostics wasn't available here, so nothing was type-checked. Everything below comes from reading code, logs and the session transcript.\n\n### What the evidence shows (verified)\n\nThe best evidence is pi's own transcript: `~/Library/Application Support/DefaultCompany/unity/pi-home/sessions/--Users-youxun-Library-Application Support-DefaultCompany-unity-pi-home--/2026-10-17T11-21-22-354Z_companion.jsonl`. I summarized every assistant turn in it:\n\n| time (UTC) | stopReason | content | output tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 11:21:30 | stop | thinking 1533 chars + **text** (valid JSON) | 948 |\n| 11:21:44 | **length** | thinking only, **no text** | 1962 |\n| 11:22:11 | **length** | thinking only | 1926 |\n| 11:40:57 to 11:49:06 (5 turns) | **length** | thinking only | 1322–1726 |\n\nWhat this tells us:\n- **Unity's stdin works.** The prompts arrive intact (Chinese text, newlines, quotes), and so does `--session-id companion`, because pi logged \"No project session found with id 'companion'\". So `ArgumentList`, the stdin encoding and BOM, the flush, the PATH (`/opt/homebrew/bin/node` resolves for pi's `#!/usr/bin/env node` script) and the space in \"Application Support\" all work. **Hypothesis (1), Mono Process behaviour, is ruled out as the root cause.**\n- **pi does answer, but `--thinking off` doesn't stop the model thinking.** pi leaves the reasoning parameter out when thinking is off, and Ollama's OpenAI-compatible `/v1` endpoint lets thinking models think by default. The model then spends its whole `maxTokens: 2048` budget on reasoning and stops with `length` before writing any text.\n- **Timeline for botB:**\n  - Run 1 greet: answered in 8s.\n  - Run 1 reflect: `agent_end` after 13s with no text, so `result = null` and the fallback was used (log line 471, no timeout).\n  - Nemesis, running at the same time: timed out (line 485).\n  - Run 2 greet: waited behind the `busy` gate, answered in 15s with no text.\n  - Run 2 reflect: sent at 11:22:11.110 and never answered within 45s (line 558).\n- Each call generates about 2,000 tokens, and three things compete for one Ollama instance: two pi channels plus KevScorer on the same `tev1:0.8b` model. Ollama works through them one at a time, so calls queue past 45s. In botD, KevScorer's own 2s requests also time out (\"Curl error 28 … 0 bytes received\", log lines 408 and 444), which shows Ollama was saturated.\n- The only stderr pi printed was that session-creation warning. Nothing else.\n\n### Issues (ranked)\n\n**[CRITICAL] The model never produces text: thinking fills the token budget**\nFile: `Assets/Scripts/Game/Agents/PiHost.cs:43, 58`, with the effect at `PiRpcChannel.cs:73, 86`\nConfidence: HIGH (verified in the transcript)\n- **Scenario:** every call after the first ends `stopReason=length` with only thinking. `text.Length == 0`, so `result = null` and the rule-based fallback always wins. \"Empty text\" is therefore the normal outcome, not just a symptom of the timeouts.\n- **Fix:** turn thinking off on the Ollama side. Options:\n  - Use an Ollama model or Modelfile that doesn't think.\n  - Have pi send `reasoning_effort: \"none\"`. Ollama's `/v1` endpoint maps that to `think:false`; this needs a pi provider/compat option, so check `packages/ai` openai-completions.\n  - Use the native `/api/chat` with `think:false`.\n  - As a stopgap: lower `maxTokens` (around 256) so calls finish fast, and add `/no_think` to the system prompt if the model honours it.\n- Also log `stopReason` and the thinking length when `agent_end` arrives with empty text, so this failure is visible and not silently swallowed.\n\n**[HIGH] Ollama overload: two pi channels plus KevScorer on one model**\nFile: `GameApp.cs:25-35`, `AgentCoordinator.cs:41, 53`\nConfidence: HIGH that they compete (Curl 28 in botD, nemesis timing out while companion is generating); MEDIUM that this alone pushes calls past 45s.\n- **Scenario:** at the end of a run, nemesis Refine and companion Say start together, and KevScorer keeps firing during play. With about 2,000 tokens per pi call, the second request in the queue easily waits more than 45s.\n- **Fix:** fixing the CRITICAL issue removes most of this. In addition, run the agent calls one at a time through a single shared gate (one Ollama request in flight), or skip Kev requests while a pi call is running.\n\n**[MEDIUM] The 45s timeout counts time spent waiting for the gate, and runs back-to-back on one channel**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:56, 77`, `AgentCoordinator.cs:27, 53`\nConfidence: HIGH (verified by reading)\n- **Scenario:** the timeout clock itself starts after the gate. But Greet for the next run waits behind the previous reflect on the same companion channel, and each can take up to 45s. A slow call therefore delays the next one by up to 45s, and by then the run may be over (batch quit, or a stale greeting).\n- **Fix:** drop or cancel a stale Ask instead of queuing it (for example, if `busy`, return null right away for Greet), or pass a deadline in from the caller.\n\n**[MEDIUM] A persistent companion session plus a reasoning model makes prompts grow**\nFile: `PiHost.cs:62`, `GameApp.cs:26`\nConfidence: MEDIUM\n- **Scenario:** every run appends turns to the `companion` session. Thinking-only turns are removed by `context_edit`, but successful ones (with their thinking) stay. As prompt evaluation grows, calls slow down; the transcript shows `input` rising to 982 tokens.\n- **Fix:** keep it stateless (`--no-session`, like nemesis), because memory already lives in the save file and goes into the prompt. Or cap and compact the session.\n\n**[LOW] The first `agent_end` ends the wait, even if pi retries**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:74`\nConfidence: MEDIUM (`agent-session.ts:1144` emits `agent_end` with `willRetry`)\n- **Scenario:** on a provider error that pi retries, the first `agent_end` has `willRetry: true`. Ask stops there with empty text, and the retry's output lands in the queue, where the next Ask's drain discards it.\n- **Fix:** add `public bool willRetry;` to `Ev` and treat `agent_end` as final only when `!willRetry`.\n\n**[LOW] A pi error response to the prompt is ignored, so the call waits the full 45s**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:69-75`\nConfidence: MEDIUM\n- **Scenario:** if preflight fails (bad model or provider), pi replies `{\"type\":\"response\",\"command\":\"prompt\",\"success\":false,\"error\":...}` and may never emit `agent_end`. Ask then waits the whole 45s and logs \"timeout\".\n- **Fix:** add `success` and `error` fields to `Ev`. On `type==\"response\" &amp;&amp; !success`, log the error and end right away.\n\n**[LOW] Stale output from a killed process can leak into the next Ask**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:35, 63, 97-98`\nConfidence: LOW (speculative)\n- **Scenario:** after `Kill()`, the old process's async reader can still enqueue buffered lines, including an `agent_end`, after the next Ask's drain at line 63. That would end the new wait early with empty text. The window is small because the old process is already dead.\n- **Fix:** give each process its own queue (create a new `ConcurrentQueue` in `EnsureStarted` and capture it in the lambda), or filter on a generation counter.\n\n**[LOW] Killed or exited `Process` objects are never disposed**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:95-98`\nConfidence: HIGH\n- **Scenario:** each restart leaks a `Process` handle along with its reader threads and event subscriptions. Small, but it adds up across many timeouts.\n- **Fix:** call `proc.Dispose()` after `Kill()`, and also when `HasExited` is detected in `EnsureStarted`.\n\n**[LOW] Timeout accumulated from `Time.unscaledDeltaTime`**\nFile: `PiRpcChannel.cs:66, 77`\nConfidence: HIGH that it's correct; LOW that it causes any problem.\n- `unscaledDeltaTime` ignores `timeScale=4` and is real time in batchmode, so this is not a cause.\n- **Fix (robustness only):** compute the deadline from `Time.realtimeSinceStartupAsDouble` (or a `Stopwatch`) so frame stalls or clamping can't skew it.\n\n**[LOW] Process not killed on domain reload (Editor only)**\nFile: `GameApp.cs:69`\nConfidence: MEDIUM\n- **Scenario:** `OnDestroy` covers leaving playmode and quitting. A script recompile while in playmode, or an Editor crash, can orphan the `node` pi processes.\n- **Fix:** also hook `AppDomain.CurrentDomain.DomainUnload` / `AssemblyReloadEvents.beforeAssemblyReload` to call `pi?.Dispose()`.\n\n**[LOW] Model name concatenated into hand-built JSON**\nFile: `PiHost.cs:42-43`\nConfidence: HIGH\n- **Scenario:** an `AGENT_MODEL` value containing `\"` or `\\` produces an invalid `models.json`.\n- **Fix:** escape it, or build the file with a serializable class and `JsonUtility`.\n\n### Checked and ruled out (verified)\n- **Stdin side:** `ArgumentList` quoting of the system prompt, and `StandardInputEncoding = new UTF8Encoding(false)` (no BOM). pi's own JSONL reader splits on `\\n`, and Mono `WriteLine` on macOS writes `\\n`.\n- **Output side:** `Flush` after each write, and `Encoding.UTF8` on stdout.\n- **Paths:** the space in the working-directory path, and the PATH that resolves `node`.\n- **Parsing:** `JsonUtility` on event shapes it doesn't model: unknown fields are ignored, and non-JSON lines are caught and become `null`.\n- **Coroutine structure:** `yield` inside `try/finally` is allowed in iterators; `busy` is always reset; the `break` at line 74 only leaves stale lines, which the next drain discards.\n- **Draining at the start of Ask:** it runs before `Send`, so it can't drop a reply to the current prompt.\n- **`HasExited`:** behaves as expected.\n- **Process start:** a failure to start or an early exit would show as \"process exited\" or \"start failed\", and neither appears in the logs.\n\n### Open Questions\n- **[MEDIUM, LOW confidence] Python vs Unity:** \"The same invocation works from Python in 2-10s\" is probably a single call with Ollama otherwise idle, and/or a short prompt. The `probe-x` session (11:42:43) answered with text after 668 chars of thinking. The difference is load and prompt length, not the process plumbing. To confirm, run the Python harness with nemesis and companion at the same time and Kev traffic running alongside.\n\n### Positive Observations\n- An isolated `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` and its own `models.json` keep the game away from the user's global pi state.\n- One prompt at a time per channel, kill-and-restart on a hang, and the `finally` that resets `busy` make for a sound, simple design.\n- The rule-based plan is applied immediately and the LLM result only upgrades it, so these failures degrade gracefully and never block a run.\n- `GameApp.OnDestroy` disposes `PiHost`, so pi subprocesses are cleaned up on normal exit.\n\n### Recommendation\n**REQUEST CHANGES.** In order:\n1. Stop the model thinking (or cap `maxTokens`), and log `stopReason` when the text is empty.\n2. Allow only one Ollama request at a time across nemesis, companion and Kev.\n3. Handle `willRetry` and prompt error responses in `PiRpcChannel`.\n4. Then do the small lifecycle fixes (per-process queue, Dispose, domain reload).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>86820</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>178653</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "还有什么可以并行的,不需要我决策,不依赖前面跑出来的,并行去干吧,尤其素材什么的,还要下载把", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab8aa0304c53b95f6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NZkMu1kpMWEaatu6uTZLfC</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/ab8aa0304c53b95f6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Write architecture docs and CLAUDE.md\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>COMPLETED TASK: Write project documentation for `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite` (CLAUDE.md, docs/README.md, docs/architecture/overview.md, docs/specs/agent-layer.md, docs/proposals/README.md). Prose in Chinese, identifiers in English. No code edits, no git commits.\n\nSTATUS: SUCCESS (docs written and checked against code; the one change I made after writing was a text correction pass on the spec and overview)\n\nFILES CHANGED:\n- Created: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/CLAUDE.md`\n- Created: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/docs/README.md`\n- Created: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/docs/architecture/overview.md`\n- Created: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/docs/specs/agent-layer.md`\n- Created: `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite/docs/proposals/README.md`\n- Modified: none. `docs/assets/` was not touched.\n\nNote: the environment said this is not a git repo, but `git status` works. The tree already had unrelated changes that are not mine: a modified `.omc/state/hud-stdin-cache.json`, an untracked `.omc/.../last-tool-error-state.json`, and an untracked `assets-src/`.\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Code examples tested: 2/2 command blocks run. The EditMode command ran in a scratch copy and passed 50/50 (exit 0; the log shows only Unity licensing network noise). The bot command ran in the scratch copy and printed `[PLAN-RULE]`, `[RUN]`, `[PLAN] llm=False`, `[COMPANION]`, and `[BOT] finished`. The bot run used `AGENT_NO_LLM=1`, so the LLM path was not exercised headlessly.\n- Commands verified: 2/2 valid. Note that `~/.unity/bin/Unity` is a CLI wrapper, not the editor. The editor is `/Applications/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.4.8f1/Unity.app/Contents/MacOS/Unity`, and CLAUDE.md uses that path.\n- Not verified: the kev/systemone endpoint. No server implementation exists in the repo, so the request and parse format is documented from `KevScorer` and its tests only. This is stated in spec section 7.5.\n- The ECS rationale in spec 8.1 is inferred from code structure and the manifest, because the repo does not state it. This is marked as inferred.\n\nInconsistencies and undocumented behaviour found in the code:\n1. `AGENT_LLM_URL` affects only kev. pi's endpoint is hard-coded to `http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1` in `PiHost.WriteModels`. This is now documented in CLAUDE.md.\n2. `NemesisBrain.Refine` sets `fromLlm = true` as soon as JSON parses, even if `Sanitize` replaces the whole sequence with the fallback. So `[PLAN] llm=True` does not prove the LLM plan was used. Documented in spec 2.3.\n3. `TacticScript.Pick` is called only from tests. Production uses `RuleScorer` → `TacticScript.Eval`.\n4. `PiHost.Open` has a `--session-id` branch, but `GameApp` always passes `null`, so every call is `--no-session`.\n5. Prompt length limits do not match the code. Companion prompt says 30 characters, code truncates at 50. Nemesis prompt says 40, code truncates at 60.\n6. `Core` asmdef does not set `noEngineReferences`, and Core uses `UnityEngine` types (`Mathf`, `JsonUtility`, `Debug`). So \"engine-light\" is partly true. Documented in CLAUDE.md and the overview.\n7. `BuildTools.RunBot` does not check `AGENT_BOT`. It only enters Play mode, and the bot is enabled by the environment variable inside `GameApp`.\n8. PLAN vs code gaps are listed as proposals P1–P10. The main ones are: PLAN says 5–8 rooms but `CombatRooms = 3`; no URP package in the manifest; no prefab rooms; companion behaviour intent and player commands are missing; no move cooldown field; no boss portrait close-up. The \"kev 9B evaluation\" idea is in P8. The repo has no 9B reference, and the default model is `tev1:0.8b`, not the 7–8B in PLAN.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>177000</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>42</tool_uses><duration_ms>268501</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>afb8cf9919af758c2</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ei3EKTvaDKa8EjbQMg83CA</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/afb8cf9919af758c2.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Download and catalog CC0 game assets\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All eight packs are downloaded into `assets-src/&lt;slug&gt;/`, about 340 MB in total. Nothing was imported into `unity/` and nothing was committed. I checked archive contents before extracting, and none had absolute or `..` paths or executables.\n\n**Licenses.** Every pack is CC0, so none needs attribution and nothing is CC-BY. Seven of the eight have a license file in the archive, whose text I quote in the manifest. The Quaternius monsters archive has no license file, so its CC0 status rests only on the itch.io page saying \"CC0 License\".\n\n| Pack | Slug | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| KayKit Dungeon Remastered 1.0 | `kaykit-dungeon-remastered` | 45 MB |\n| KayKit Adventurers | `kaykit-adventurers` | 119 MB |\n| KayKit Skeletons | `kaykit-skeletons` | 111 MB |\n| KayKit Character Animations 1.1 | `kaykit-character-animations` | 41 MB |\n| KayKit Forest Nature (free version) | `kaykit-forest-nature` | 13 MB |\n| Kenney UI Pack Adventure | `kenney-ui-pack-adventure` | 1.8 MB |\n| Kenney Impact Sounds | `kenney-impact-sounds` | 1.2 MB |\n| Kenney RPG Audio | `kenney-rpg-audio` | 1.1 MB |\n| Kenney Interface Sounds | `kenney-interface-sounds` | 1.1 MB |\n| Quaternius Lowpoly Animated Monsters (Bat, Dragon, Skeleton, Slime) | `quaternius-lowpoly-animated-monsters` | 6.5 MB |\n\n**Sources.** Dungeon, Adventurers and Skeletons came from the official `KayKit-Game-Assets` GitHub org by shallow clone. Character Animations, Forest Nature and the Quaternius monsters came from itch.io. The Kenney packs came from kenney.nl.\n\n**Surprises:**\n- The KayKit GitHub org has no repos for Character Animations or Forest Nature. I got those from itch.io, and plain curl was enough: there is a public download endpoint for free packs, so no browser session was needed.\n- The Adventurers and Skeletons character files already embed their own animations: 76 clips each for Adventurers and 95 each for Skeletons. The separate Character Animations pack adds 139 clips for the medium rig and 34 for the large one, including `Melee_1H_Attack_*`, `Hit_A`/`Hit_B`, `Dodge_*` for a dash, and `Skeletons_*` clips.\n- The dungeon pack has doorway walls (`wall_doorway*`) but no separate door mesh that I found.\n- Unity-friendly formats are FBX in every pack, with glTF/GLB alongside in all but the Quaternius one. Kenney audio is OGG.\n- Not obtained: KayKit Fantasy Weapons Bits, which PLAN.md lists but your list didn't include. Nothing on your list failed.\n\nI appended `assets-src/` to `.gitignore`; the existing lines are untouched. The manifest has the source URLs, formats, counts and relevant filenames for each pack.\n\nFiles are in `/Users/youxun/project/game/agent-roguelite`:\n- `docs/assets/ASSETS.md`\n- `.gitignore`\n- `assets-src/`</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>94416</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>28</tool_uses><duration_ms>286836</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>", "现在什么状况", "现在用的什么模型", "他同时具备大模型和决策的能力?", "不要有什么用什么,去找个能力最强的", "qwen3.8:27b-mxfp8这太吃性能了,估计延时很高", "找个MOE 3.6的可能现实一点", "<task-notification>\n<task-id>bxnpqgjpt</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011yuD552VfewyYSYjRQbwsQ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/bxnpqgjpt.output</output-file>\n<status>failed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"brew services restart ollama 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -1; sleep 6; /opt/homebrew/opt/ollama/bin/ollama --version 2&gt;&amp;1 | head -2; /opt/homebrew/opt/ollama/bin/ollama pull kev:9b-nvfp4 2&gt;&amp;1 | tail -3\" failed with exit code 144</summary>\n</task-notification>", "决策模型和大模型一起的,看看要一起的话,不能太大了", "不要都下下来试,找个评价最好的,速度也快的先跑"]
